@B67687 I'm not sure how can I help, I submitted a PR
you probably want to get the opencode people to respond
I've yet to be able to do this on any of my PRs and decided to stop sending them

> Please give me a minimal repro

1. Configure the MCP server (specifically taskmaster in this case) directly in .config/opencode/opencode.json
`{
"$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
    "mcp": {
      "taskmaster": {
        "type": "local",
        "command": [
          "D:/nodejs/node",
          "C:/Users/user1/AppData/Roaming/npm/node_modules/task-master-ai/dist/mcp-server.js"
        ],
        "environment": {
          "ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL": "https://api.minimax.io/anthropic",
          "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY": ""
        }
      }
    }
  }`

2. Start OpenCode
3. The MCP fails with the 30000ms error

@rekram1-node opus just compacted my chat and something he wrote on instructions stood out:

- The Edit tool in this environment strips TypeScript generic angle brackets (treats them as HTML). All file modifications involving generics must use Python or bash (not the Edit tool) to avoid corruption

dunno if that helps

I came across this comment with a solution: [anomalyco/opencode/issues/2941](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/2941#issuecomment-3572933362)

This configuration did the trick for me:
```json
{
  "provider": {
    "azure-cognitive-services": {
      "models": {
        "gpt-5.4": {
          "options": {
            "reasoningEffort": "none",
            "include": ["reasoning.encrypted_content"],
            "store": false
          }
        },
        "gpt-5.4-mini": {
          "options": {
            "reasoningEffort": "none",
            "include": ["reasoning.encrypted_content"],
            "store": false
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```
